  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It passes typecheck, but I haven't run `vite build` or looked at it in a browser, so the camera orbit, shadow coverage and fog density are untested.\n\n- **Instancing:** the scene has one ground plane and three instanced nodes: 8,000 trunks (cylinders), 8,000 canopies (cones) and 2,000 rocks (spheres). That is 10,000 objects drawn as three instanced calls.\n- **Placement:** a seeded LCG random generator scatters them over a disc of radius 75, so the forest is identical on every load.\n- **Colour:** canopies and rocks get a per-instance HSL colour over a white base material. Trunks share one brown.\n- **Light and fog:** one shadow-casting directional light, a hemisphere light for fill, and exponential fog at density 0.0035.\n- **Camera:** an `app.camera.setPose` call in `onFrame` moves the camera in a circle of radius 125 at height 80, at 0.08 rad/s, always looking at the forest centre. I used this instead of `interactions.orbit({ autoRotate })` because I couldn't confirm from the docs that `autoRotate` works.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on the animation frame after the first `onFrame` call.\n\n",
